# Academy Domain

## Purpose

Keep member-facing academy concepts consistent across features instead of redefining them per screen.

## When Applied

Working on member flows: booking, sessions, home, profile, maps.

## Requirements

- Reuse the shared vocabulary: member (profile), coach, session, booking, payment, subscription — model names and DB columns must match `supabase/*.sql`.
- Booking/payment/attendance flows go through RPCs (see [`data/supabase-sql.mdc`](../data/supabase-sql.mdc)).
- Read paths use cache-first (see [`data/caching-sync.mdc`](../data/caching-sync.mdc)); `booking`/`sessions` are the gold standards.
- Domain context lives in [`ai/context/`](../../../ai/context/) (booking, subscriptions, payments, attendance).

## Examples

- New "member sees session" screen → reuse `SessionModel` + `SessionsRepository`, don't remodel a session.

## Anti-patterns

- Parallel/renamed models for an existing concept (e.g. a second "session" shape).
- Encoding booking/payment business rules in a widget.

## Common Mistakes

- Skimming domain rules and duplicating pricing/subscription logic already in `lib/core/helpers/`.
- Diverging field names from the Postgres schema.
